# Boost.Geometry Documentation

## Overview
Boost.Geometry is a generic geometry library for C++. It provides a wide range of geometric operations and algorithms, including but not limited to distance calculations, area computations, intersection detection, and more. The library supports various geometric primitives such as points, lines, polygons, and boxes, and it offers both 2D and 3D geometries.

This documentation focuses on the `assign_values` algorithm, which assigns values to different types of geometries. The `assign_values` function is versatile and can handle 2D and 3D points, as well as 2D and 3D boxes and segments.

## Classes and Structs

### `detail::assign::initialize`
This struct template is used to initialize the coordinates of a geometry. It recursively sets each coordinate to a specified value.

#### Template Parameters
- `Box`: The type of the geometry being initialized.
- `Index`: The index of the current coordinate being set.
- `Dimension`: The current dimension being processed.
- `DimensionCount`: The total number of dimensions in the geometry.

#### Methods
- `static inline void apply(Box& box, coordinate_type const& value)`: Recursively initializes the coordinates of the geometry.

